<http://data.silknow.org/object/9f94e4c7-33b3-334c-9de4-37ffa79e50c3>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Man's petticoat breeches, 1660-65, English; brown and beige striped silk, lined with linen"@en , "Man’s petticoat breeches made of silk striped with brown and beige and contrasting weaves. The legs are very full, gathered into the 1⅛-inch (2.7 cm) waistband. The button stand on the left of centre front has 5 worked buttonholes. Only 1 button remains, a wooden core covered with dark beige silk. The front opening and button stand are bound with dark beige silk grosgrain ribbon. There is a pocket on each side, bound with dark beige silk grosgrain ribbon; the pocket bags are chamois. There are 4 metal hooks sewn to the waistband.\n\nThe lining has been removed. It is made of linen, with a deep border of cream and beige striped silk sewn to the lower edge, which would have turned up over the hem of the breeches."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/edc3cd27-501a-3c5f-91f0-b77b4e57fe03> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/29e049da-25d7-328b-861a-6229fccac138> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/93b3ad7e-8832-308d-bc29-7df4f6b2d943> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/063813d1-7516-3ae9-9d3d-e181345bf2bf> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Man’s petticoat breeches made of silk striped with brown and beige and contrasting weaves. The legs are very full, gathered into the 1⅛-inch (2.7 cm) waistband. The button stand on the left of centre front has 5 worked buttonholes. Only 1 button remains, a wooden core covered with dark beige silk. The front opening and button stand are bound with dark beige silk grosgrain ribbon. There is a pocket on each side, bound with dark beige silk grosgrain ribbon; the pocket bags are chamois. There are 4 metal hooks sewn to the waistband.\n\nThe lining has been removed. It is made of linen, with a deep border of cream and beige striped silk sewn to the lower edge, which would have turned up over the hem of the breeches."@en , "Man's petticoat breeches, 1660-65, English; brown and beige striped silk, lined with linen"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/9f94e4c7-33b3-334c-9de4-37ffa79e50c3/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/9f94e4c7-33b3-334c-9de4-37ffa79e50c3/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/9f94e4c7-33b3-334c-9de4-37ffa79e50c3/dimension/3> ;
