<http://data.silknow.org/object/9f94e4c7-33b3-334c-9de4-37ffa79e50c3/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man’s petticoat breeches made of silk striped with brown and beige and contrasting weaves. The legs are very full, gathered into the 1⅛-inch (2.7 cm) waistband. The button stand on the left of centre front has 5 worked buttonholes. Only 1 button remains, a wooden core covered with dark beige silk. The front opening and button stand are bound with dark beige silk grosgrain ribbon. There is a pocket on each side, bound with dark beige silk grosgrain ribbon; the pocket bags are chamois. There are 4 metal hooks sewn to the waistband.\n\nThe lining has been removed. It is made of linen, with a deep border of cream and beige striped silk sewn to the lower edge, which would have turned up over the hem of the breeches."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9f94e4c7-33b3-334c-9de4-37ffa79e50c3> .
